namespace Magma

/-- A member of the class, as the `8` orbit values it takes together with the proof that they name
one. `Magma.tupOK` is three tests: every orbit value is one the group's action allows, the operation
the tuple builds really is invariant, and no excess permutation is an automorphism of it. -/
@[reducible] def tup10R803 : Type := {w : Fin 8 → Fin 10 // Magma.tupOK S10R803.E S10R803.tr S10R803.z S10R803.st S10R803.X w = true}

/-- The class, as a family of magmas indexed by its own membership test. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def srch10R803 (v : tup10R803) : Magma (Fin 10) :=
  Magma.mk (Magma.transport S10R803.E S10R803.tr v.1)

end Magma

/-! ### The source exhibits

`5` members of the class, chosen by greedy cover so that between them they model all `31` equations
that have a model in the class at all. Each check is `Magma.tupOK`: the tuple names a member of the
class. It is `decide!` rather than `decide` because the invariance test is `100` cells times the
`27` group elements, which the elaborator will not walk inside its heartbeat limit.
-/

